I've been thinking about this too. I think it would work quite well.
You could wear earplugs to make yourself deaf on purpose, or light a
candle and then
(W)ear it to plug your ears with wax, making yourself deaf for a
limited number or turns or until you decide to knock out the wax.
Additionally, there could be another type of voice-attack monster, a
"sonic sphere"; like the other spheres, it would explode, generating a
blast of sound that would make you deaf for a certain number of turns
(and wake up every other monster on the level as well). Being struck
by lightning should also make you deaf (from the accompanying
thunder), as well as stepping on a magic trap when you are blind ("you
hear a deafening roar!") If the deafness was caused by
earplugs/candle, removing them would end the deafness (of course, if
they are cursed, you won't be able to!). Otherwise, you could cure
deafness by applying a unihorn, or eat a (giant) bat corpse (rationale
being that bats have excellent hearing, given that they navigate by
sonar. This would stun you in the process, but perhaps it would be
worth it. In any case, it would give bat corpses some use!)
Alternative scenario: bat corpses now give magical hearing, like
floating eye corpses give magical vision. If you eat a bat corpse, you
will now be able to hear voices through telepathy when deaf. However,
voice attacks (such as the Lorelei's attack discussed above) would not
harm you (because it's only in your mind, not actual sound). You would
still be unable to "hear" noises not generated by creatures with
minds, in the same way that visual telepathy only shows you monsters
with minds.

While you are deaf, you can't:
- hear level noises, squeaky boards, doors opening, etc.
- #chat to anyone
- produce an "improvise" effect on a musical instrument (perhaps you
could still play a series of predefined notes, beat a drum, or ring a
bell), or hear the sound of a musical instrument.
- hear the messages that pop up when shopkeepers, devils, guards in
Minetown, Rodney, your Quest leader, gods, etc. try to talk to you
- buy anything from a shop (if you can't hear, how are you going to
ask the price?)
- hear magic trap effects ("You hear a deafening roar"/"You hear
distant howling")
- hear a "CRASH!" when breaking something with force bolt/wand of
striking, "splat!", or other assorted noises
- hear a cockatrice's hissing (and therefore won't be stoned!)
- successfully get a wish after releasing a djinni from a lamp (you
won't hear what it's saying, so it will just give up and go away)

I think that covers most of it -- anything else?

